senses.gloss:
उ॑ल्ब or उ॑ल्व (rarely अस्, m.), अम्, n. (√ उच्, ‘to accumulate’, Uṇ. iv, 95; more probably fr. √ 1. वृ, BRD.), a cover, envelope, esp. the membrane surrounding the embryo, RV. x, 51, 1; AV. iv, 2, 8; VS.; TS.; ŚBr. &c.;
 the vulva, womb, VS. xix, 76;
 a cave, cavity, L.;
 [cf. Lat. alvus, vulva; Lith. urwā, üla.]

उल्ब॑ण or उल्व॑ण, n. the membrane enveloping the embryo, TĀr. i, 10, 7
 (उल्बण॑) mfn. anything laid over in addition, superfluous, abundant, excessive, much, immense, strong, powerful, TS. iii; MBh.; BhP.; Suśr. &c.;
 singular, strange, AitĀr.;
 manifest, evident, L.
 (ifc.) abundantly furnished with, MBh.; Suśr. &c.;
 (अस्), m. a particular position of the hands in dancing;
 N. of a son of Vasiṣṭha, BhP.;
 (आ), f. a particular dish (consisting of milk mixed with the juice of melons, bananas &c.), Nigh.

